  "body": "AGENTS.md \"400-line files\" now exempts post-processor scripts (`assets/posts/*.cps`): a post script is one file the post engine loads and runs for one machine dialect, so it stays whole at whatever length its dialect needs; reviews judge it for correctness, not length.\n\nUser, 2026-11-08: \"CPS files cannot follow the 400 line rules as its a script to be executed by a post processor, and it needs what it needs.. (this should be in the 400line law)\"\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
